    {
      "text": "####fill\n\n`Using the fill function, you can fill one or more columns with a set of values`\n\n1. df.na.fill(\"All Null values become this string\")  :   all null vaues become passed string\n2. df.na.fill(5, Seq(\"StockCode\", \"InvoiceNo\")) :  all the null value of for provided seq of columns would becom 5\n3. val fillColValues = Map(\"StockCode\" -> 5, \"Description\" -> \"No Value\")\n\n       df.na.fill(fillColValues)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "ef8823529a6b41288c5d4"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nval complexDF = retailDF.withColumn(\"complex_map\",f.map(f.col(\"Description\"), f.col(\"InvoiceNo\")))\n.select(f.col(\"Description\"), f.col(\"invoiceno\"), f.col(\"complex_map\"),f.col(\"complex_map\").getField(\"CITRONELLA CANDLE FLOWERPOT\")\n)\ncomplexDF.show(2,false)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
