    {
      "text": "### Working with null values\n\n1. coalesce(col(\"Description\"), col(\"CustomerId\")) : select the first non-null value from a set of columns \n2. ifnull, nullIf, nvl, and nvl2\n3. \n```\nalways use nulls to represent missing or empty data in your\nDataFrames. Spark can optimize working with null values more than it can if you use empty\nstrings or other values\n\ndf.na._\n1. There are two things you can do with null values: you can explicitly drop nulls or you can fill\nthem with a value (globally or on a per-column basis)\n```",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "0fc5dc158e2a4202af396"
    },
    {
      "text": "\n###Working with Complex Types\n\n>There are three kinds of complex types: structs, arrays,\nand maps.",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "e51c69eb63044eda8b154"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nval structDF = retailDF.select(f.struct(\"Description\", \"InvoiceNo\").alias(\"complex\"))\n\nstructDF.select(f.col(\"complex\").getField(\"description\"), f.col(\"complex\")).show(5,false)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "49274c3156f94d3b88a73"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\ndef power3(number:Double):Double = number * number * number\npower3(2.0)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
