    },
    {
      "text": "\n###replace\n\n> this work with other values as well\n`There are more flexible\noptions that you can use with more than just null values. Probably the most common use case is\nto replace all values in a certain column according to their current value`\n\n1. df.na.replace(\"Description\", Map(\"\" -> \"UNKNOWN\"))  :  replace empty string with uknown for column description\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "0fa611d4836c4ba8801f6"
    },
