    {
      "text": "\n###drop\n`drop, which removes rows that contain nulls. `\n\n1. df.na.drop(\"any\")  : this is default behaviour, if any column has null value it will drop entire row\n2. df.na.drop(\"all\"):  if all the column has null value then only drop the row\n3. df.na.drop(\"all\", Seq(\"StockCode\", \"InvoiceNo\")):  if selected columns has null value , then only drop the row\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
