    {
      "text": "###User defined function\n\n>user-defined functions (UDFs) make it possible for you to write your own custom\ntransformations using Python or Scala and even use external libraries. \n\n1. create a function\n2. register with myudf = f.udf(f:Int=>Double)\n3. call on column  myudf(col(\"test\"))\n\n`Note:\n\nif you want to use in expr or in sql  we can also register this UDF as a\nSpark SQL function\n\nspark.udf.register(\"power3\", power3(_:Double):Double)`",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
